d:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-12 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Bottom line"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-fg-muted leading-relaxed","children":"Hotjar and Nebula solve different problems at different stages. Hotjar is a post-launch optimisation tool - you need traffic, time, and sessions to get actionable data. Nebula is a pre-conversion diagnostic - it checks whether the page's conversion signals pass before you spend another dollar on ads. If your page has a message-match failure or a weak CTA, Hotjar will show you people leaving. Nebula identifies the failing signal before they arrive."}]]}]
